# What is deliberately NOT pushed, and how to get it back.
#
# The whole tree is ~629 MB, and most of that is regenerable. What is left
# after these rules is ~74 MB: every source file, every document, every
# model, and the measurements behind them - enough to compile the exact EA
# that shipped, on a clean machine, without retraining anything.
#
# Delete any rule below if you would rather have that category on GitHub.

# Compiler output (~205 MB). Rebuilt by compiling MintyAI.mq5 in MetaEditor.
# The .ex5 also breaches GitHub's 50 MB advisory on its own - it carries all
# 37 models inside it.
*.ex5

# Exported price history (~226 MB). Regenerate with
# Scripts\MintyAI\MintyAIExportAll.mq5 against your broker.
*_bars.csv

# Feature-parity dumps. Rebuilt by the same export script.
*_features_mql5.csv

# PyTorch weights (~74 MB). Only needed to re-derive risk presets from an
# existing model - python -m mintyai.retune. The .onnx files ARE the
# shipping models and are kept.
*.pt

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
